  "mechanisms": {
    "entry": "wow_control_client_procedure selects list_entryA/W or combo_list_entryA/W, all using edit_entry. Existing owner binds current task, retains window words and borrow scope, captures TLS metrics, invokes original procedure, restores TLS and releases words before leaving scopes in finally. Terminal finalization avoids fresh metric capture. This is current mechanism evidence, not approval of every guard.",
    "allocation": "Original VALIDATECLASSANDSIZE and INITCONTROLLOOKASIDE in C usercli.h own FNID/size/no-allocation policy, original InitLookaside and AllocLookasideEntry resolve C rtlinit.obj. ListboxLookaside is defined by lb1.c. gcWheelDelta is original C globals.h/clglobal.c common storage, not TLS metric state or an F-owned allocation. Common map labels alone do not prove an F owner.",
    "style": "Original WM_NCCREATE computes multicolumn style mask. F wow_edit_alter_window_style calls already-B native NtUserAlterWindowStyle and refreshes the retained WND. Public SetWindowLong adds distinct notification behavior; moving this C-layout refresh into B is not an in-place solution. Review shared owner in S13.",
    "privateWords": "Original initialization stores PLBIV through mapped setter -> validate HWND -> C xxxSetWindowLong; FNID provider derives original kernel/ntstubs.c. Registered extent depends on original WND/LBWND expressions. S14 must compare existing extracted units and measure proposed C restoration, not invent duplicate layouts.",
    "drawing": "Original procedure uses provided DC or BeginPaint/EndPaint, tracks capture and delegates mouse policy to original list bodies. FillWindow/native return and SendMessageW stay shared control boundaries, not new per-ListBox wrappers.",
    "strings": "Actual MBToWCSEx resolves non-mvdm/windows/core/ntuser/rtl/chartran.c; native locale validation, heap free and KillTimer stay SDK imports. No new encoding or timer subsystem needed.",
    "messages": "FWINDOWMSG reads existing wow_default_message_state initialized through original InitMessageTables. C owns the filter algorithm; table storage/initialization is S14 shared cohort.",
    "method": "Read complete835-line lb1.c; decode actual production COFF and VALID dependencies, correlate every undefined symbol against final map, inspect original macros and current entry/state/extent/native-return providers. No new execution test."
  },
